        "reasoning_text": "The agents are still running. Let me start building the changes.json and planning the release notes while waiting. I have enough data from the runtime and other-changes agents to start.Let me now:\n1. Create the preview3 directory structure\n2. Build a preliminary changes.json based on what I have\n3. Start scoring the features for features.json\n4. Start writing the markdown release notes\n\nLet me first assess the key user-facing changes I've identified:\n\n**HIGH SCORE (7-9):**\n1. `runtime-async enabled for net11.0 shared framework` (runtime #126343) - This is a huge milestone - runtime async is now enabled by default for framework projects targeting net11.0! Score: 9\n\n\n2. `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` (runtime #124644) - New System.Text.Json naming policy. Score: 7\n3. `Add unsafe evolution attributes` (runtime #125721) - Part of the Unsafe Evolution preview feature. Score: 7\n\n**MEDIUM SCORE (4-6):**\n4. `TarWriter: use HardLink entries for hard-linked files` (runtime #123874) - Notable tar improvement that fixes how hard-linked files are handled. Score: 4\n5. `Synchronize PaxTarEntry ExtendedAttributes` (runtime #123990) - Tar fix for extended attributes. Score: 3\n6. `Relax RandomAccess type requirements` (runtime #125512) - Enables non-seekable files to work with RandomAccess APIs. Score: 5\n7. `Allow null arguments in ProcessStartInfo` (runtime #126076) - Improves nullable reference type support. Score: 5\n8. `Fix IndexOutOfRangeException in FrozenHashTable` (runtime #125555) - Addresses a critical bug in the frozen hash table implementation. Score: 4\n9. `Improve HashSet<T> performance` (runtime #125893) - Optimizes JIT bounds check elimination for collection operations. Score: 5\n10. `JIT: skip saving unmutated locals in reused continuations` (runtime #125615) - JIT optimization that reduces overhead in async scenarios. Score: 6\n11. `Add VectorXx.Asin + TensorPrimitives.Asin` (runtime #126052) - Adds inverse sine math APIs for vectors and tensors. Score: 5\n12. `Fix broadcast output shape computation in tensor binary operations` (runtime #125582) - Corrects shape calculation for tensor operations. Score: 3\n13. `Annotate System.Speech for nullable reference types` (runtime #119564) - Adds nullable annotations to the Speech library. Score: 4\n14. `Fix Saf` - Entry appears incomplete.\n\nLooking at the lower-scoring items and other repos: there are several internal APIs and infrastructure changes that don't warrant inclusion, plus some specialized areas like WASM. For EF Core, the Cosmos session token tracking and platform-specific app warnings are solid improvements, though the SqlClient update is more incremental. The SDK has a useful fix for project reference handling across different target frameworks. Roslyn's LSP TypeHierarchy support is more of a tooling boundary question, and F# mostly shows workflow-related changes that need clearer context.\n\nNow I'm ready to structure the release notes with what I've gathered so far, and I'll fill in gaps as the remaining analysis comes through.",
