ativeAOT publishing to handle satellite assemblies correctly, optimizing MetadataBuilder.GetOrAddConstantBlob, and improving runtime-async support for the linux-riscv64 architecture. Now looking at the MSBuild changes. Looking at the rest of the MSBuild fixes, there are several more critical issues being addressed around file handling, metadata preservation, and task host compatibility across different platforms. On the NuGet side, there are security improvements for alias validation, better audit suppression handling, and new CLI features for signing and framework-aware packing. The Razor changes appear to be mostly IDE-focused tooling updates.\n\nFor the remaining areas, templating is getting AOT compatibility improvements and duplicate key fixes, WPF has minimal changes, and EF Core is addressing Cosmos session token tracking and updating SQL Client dependencies.\n\nF# changes are mostly infrastructure work rather than language features, while WinForms has a couple of bug fixes around control destruction and ComboBox item handling.\n\nNow I need to pull the ASP.NET Core data and start drafting the actual release notes.",
