            "function": {
              "name": "create",
              "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/write_files.py\", \"file_text\": \"import os\\n\\nbase = \\\"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/preview3\\\"\\nos.makedirs(base, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nfiles = {}\\n\\nfiles[\\\"README.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# .NET 11 Preview 3 - Release Notes\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 release notes. Find more information on new features released in .NET 11 Preview 3 by browsing through the release notes below:\\n\\n- [Libraries](./libraries.md)\\n- [Runtime](./runtime.md)\\n- [SDK](./sdk.md)\\n- [MSBuild](./msbuild.md)\\n\\n## Languages\\n\\n- [C#](./csharp.md)\\n- [F#](./fsharp.md)\\n- [Visual Basic](./visualbasic.md)\\n\\n## Workloads, Libraries, & More\\n\\n- [.NET MAUI](./dotnetmaui.md)\\n- [ASP.NET Core](./aspnetcore.md)\\n- [Container images](./containers.md)\\n- [EF Core & Data](./efcore.md)\\n- [NuGet](./nuget.md)\\n- [Windows Forms](./winforms.md)\\n- [WPF](./wpf.md)\\n\\n## Get Started\\n\\nInstructions on getting started with .NET 11 can be found in the [getting started guide](../../get-started.md). Installers and binaries for .NET 11 Preview 3 can be found [here on GitHub](./11.0.0-preview.3.md).\\n\\n## Stay up-to-date\\n\\nYou can find a detailed overview of all new features in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in C#](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/)\\n- [What's new in .NET MAUI](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/maui/whats-new/)\\n- [What's new in Entity Framework Core](https://learn.microsoft.com/ef/core/what-is-new/)\\n- [What's new in Windows Forms](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/desktop/winforms/whats-new/)\\n- [What's new in WPF](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/desktop/wpf/whats-new/)\\n\\nThe latest .NET 11 release is always available at [dotnet.microsoft.com](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/11.0) and [.NET 11 Releases](../../README.md).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"runtime.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# .NET Runtime in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## Runtime Async now enabled by default for net11.0+\\n\\nPreview 3 marks a milestone for runtime-async: it is now enabled by default for all shared framework projects targeting `net11.0` and later. In previous previews, runtime-async required explicit compiler feature flags and `EnablePreviewFeatures`. Starting in Preview 3, shared framework source projects — including the core libraries — build with runtime-async enabled automatically.\\n\\nThis change means that more of the class libraries you call every day are now compiled as runtime-async methods. The result is cleaner stack traces and lower overhead across the board, not just in code you write yourself.\\n\\nUser code still requires the preview opt-in to emit `MethodImplOptions.Async` methods. The feature remains a preview, and the compiler flag is still required to author runtime-async methods:\\n\\n```xml\\n<PropertyGroup>\\n  <Features>runtime-async=on</Features>\\n  <EnablePreviewFeatures>true</EnablePreviewFeatures>\\n</PropertyGroup>\\n```\\n\\nFor more on runtime-async, see the [Preview 2 notes](../preview2/runtime.md#runtime-async-v2) for the full introduction.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#126343](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126343)\\n\\n### JIT optimizations for runtime-async continuations\\n\\nTwo JIT improvements reduce the overhead of async suspension when continuation objects are reused:\\n\\n- **Skip saving unmutated locals** — when a method's local variables have not changed since suspension, the JIT skips writing them back into the continuation heap object. ([dotnet/runtime#125615](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125615))\\n- **Null out exception slots in reused continuations** — clearing the exception field in recycled continuation objects allows the GC to collect stale exception references sooner, and reenables safe continuation reuse. ([dotnet/runtime#125869](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125869))\\n\\nBoth optimizations apply automatically with no code changes required.\\n\\n## Unsafe Evolution (preview)\\n\\n> **Note:** This is a preview feature for .NET 11.\\n\\nPreview 3 adds the unsafe evolution attribute types needed to annotate members participating in the Unsafe Evolution feature. This design provides a safe, declared path for library authors to expose access to otherwise-private members without reflection, building on top of the `[UnsafeAccessor]` attribute introduced in .NET 8.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#125721](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125721)\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed an `IndexOutOfRangeException` in `FrozenHashTable` when creating a frozen collection from a very large input. ([dotnet/runtime#125555](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125555))\\n- Fixed a `SafeFileHandle.CanSeek` performance regression. ([dotnet/runtime#125807](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125807))\\n- Fixed `SingleConsumerUnboundedChannel.WaitToReadAsync` returning an exception instead of `false` after the writer completes. ([dotnet/runtime#125745](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125745))\\n- Fixed `ErrorOnUnknownConfiguration` not respecting `ConfigurationKeyNameAttribute` when validating options. ([dotnet/runtime#125876](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125876))\\n- Fixed an out-of-memory error in `BinHexDecoder`, `Base64Decoder`, and `XmlSchemaValidator` when they throw on large invalid input. ([dotnet/runtime#125930](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125930))\\n- Fixed NativeAOT publish incorrectly including satellite assemblies despite them being embedded. ([dotnet/runtime#124192](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124192))\\n- Fixed an RCW cache entry leak when releasing COM wrapper objects. ([dotnet/runtime#125754](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125754))\\n- Fixed `ImmutableArray<T>.Builder.RemoveAll` missing a null check on the predicate. ([dotnet/runtime#125920](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125920))\\n- Thread names longer than 15 characters are now truncated before being passed to `pthread_setname_np` on Linux, avoiding silent failures. ([dotnet/runtime#125928](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125928))\\n- Improved error handling in OpenSSL initialization code. ([dotnet/runtime#125324](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125324))\\n- Improved runtime-async support on linux-riscv64. ([dotnet/runtime#125446](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125446))\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\n- `HashSet<T>` lookup performance improved by enabling JIT bounds-check elimination for internal bucket indexing. ([dotnet/runtime#125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893))\\n- `ActivatorUtilities.CreateInstance` now defers `GetServiceInfo` initialization until first use, reducing startup overhead for DI-heavy applications. ([dotnet/runtime#126005](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126005))\\n- `MetadataBuilder.GetOrAddConstantBlob` in the System.Reflection.Metadata package is optimized to reduce allocations when encoding constant values. ([dotnet/runtime#121223](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/121223))\\n\\n## Community contributors\\n\\nThank you to everyone who contributed to the .NET Runtime in Preview 3.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"libraries.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# .NET Libraries in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase\\n\\n`System.Text.Json` gains a new built-in naming policy: `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase`. This mirrors the existing `JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` and converts property names to PascalCase (e.g., `firstName` becomes `FirstName`).\\n\\n```csharp\\nvar options = new JsonSerializerOptions\\n{\\n    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase\\n};\\n\\nstring json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new { firstName = \\\"Ada\\\", lastName = \\\"Lovelace\\\" }, options);\\n// {\\\"FirstName\\\":\\\"Ada\\\",\\\"LastName\\\":\\\"Lovelace\\\"}\\n```\\n\\nThe corresponding `JsonKnownNamingPolicy.PascalCase` enum value is also added for use with `[JsonSourceGenerationOptions]`.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#124644](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124644)\\n\\n## RandomAccess works with non-seekable files\\n\\n`RandomAccess.Read` and `RandomAccess.Write` previously required the underlying `SafeFileHandle` to be seekable. In Preview 3 this requirement is relaxed: both methods now work with non-seekable handles such as pipes and character devices.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#125512](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125512)\\n\\n## TarWriter: correct HardLink entries for hard-linked files\\n\\nWhen `TarWriter` encounters multiple filesystem entries that share the same inode (hard links), it now writes them using `TarEntryType.HardLink` entries after the first occurrence rather than duplicating the file content. This matches standard tar behavior and produces smaller archives.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#123874](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123874)\\n\\n## PaxTarEntry extended attributes synchronized with property setters\\n\\nSetting `PaxTarEntry` properties such as `ModificationTime` and `UserName` now immediately updates the underlying `ExtendedAttributes` dictionary. Previously the two could go out of sync.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#123990](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123990)\\n\\n## Vector Asin and vectorized TensorPrimitives.Asin\\n\\n`Vector128<T>`, `Vector256<T>`, `Vector512<T>`, and `Vector64<T>` gain `Asin` methods. `TensorPrimitives.Asin` is vectorized using these new APIs, accelerating batched inverse-sine operations on supported hardware.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#126052](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126052)\\n\\n## Nullable annotations for System.Speech\\n\\n`System.Speech` is now fully annotated for nullable reference types, improving the experience for projects that enable `<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#119564](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/119564)\\n\\n## ProcessStartInfo accepts null arguments\\n\\n`ProcessStartInfo` constructor overloads and `Process.Start` now accept `null` for the `arguments` parameter, aligning with the nullable reference type annotations on the API.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/runtime#126076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126076)\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"aspnetcore.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# ASP.NET Core in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## Blazor Virtualize: variable-height items\\n\\nThe `Virtualize` component now supports items of different heights. Previously, `Virtualize` required all items to be the same height (`ItemSize`). In Preview 3, the component measures each item's actual rendered height, enabling smooth scrolling through heterogeneous lists.\\n\\n```razor\\n<Virtualize Items=\\\"@items\\\" Context=\\\"item\\\">\\n    <ItemContent>\\n        <div class=\\\"item @(item.IsExpanded ? \\\"expanded\\\" : \\\"\\\")\\\">\\n            <p>@item.Title</p>\\n            @if (item.IsExpanded)\\n            {\\n                <p>@item.Body</p>\\n            }\\n        </div>\\n    </ItemContent>\\n</Virtualize>\\n```\\n\\nVariable-height virtualization is enabled automatically when `ItemSize` is not set. The component measures each rendered item and updates its scroll size estimates as the user scrolls.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/aspnetcore#64964](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64964)\\n\\n## zstd Content-Encoding support\\n\\nASP.NET Core's response compression middleware and static file serving now accept and produce `zstd` (Zstandard) `Content-Encoding`. Zstandard offers better compression ratios than gzip at similar or faster speeds. When a client sends `Accept-Encoding: zstd`, the server can respond with Zstandard-compressed content.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/aspnetcore#65479](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65479)\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed a crash in `ManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor` caused by incorrect calculations. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65890](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65890))\\n- Fixed HTTP/2 `Content-Length` mismatch when trailers are split across `CONTINUATION` frames. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65765](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65765))\\n- Fixed HTTP/3 not processing requests while waiting for the peer's control stream, improving startup latency on new connections. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65399](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65399))\\n- Fixed `HPack`/`QPack` decoder limit validation after decoding variable-length integers. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65771](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65771))\\n- Fixed `StatefulReconnect` cancellation handling that could leave SignalR connections in a broken state. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65732](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65732))\\n- Fixed `TempData` lazy-loading bugs where values could be lost on first access. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65722](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65722))\\n- Fixed `Virtualize` scroll container detection when the container has horizontal overflow. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65744](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65744))\\n- Fixed a null reference exception in the `Virtualize` component during initial render. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65207](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65207))\\n- Fixed an `IJSObjectReference` memory leak in `ResourceCollectionProvider`. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65606](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65606))\\n- Fixed Blazor resource collection endpoint returning incorrect `Cache-Control` headers. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65513](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65513))\\n- Fixed the Blazor WASM Web Worker template failing to start in published apps. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65885](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65885))\\n- Fixed oversized TLS record length handling in `TlsListener`. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65558](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65558))\\n- Fixed `JsonPatchDocument` operation application bug. ([dotnet/aspnetcore#65470](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/65470))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"efcore.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# EF Core in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## Cosmos DB: session token tracking for failure recovery\\n\\nEF Core's Cosmos DB provider now tracks session tokens for requests that fail with `PreconditionFailed`, `Conflict`, or `NotFound` HTTP status codes. These failures carry a response session token that reflects the server's current state. Capturing that token lets EF Core resume a consistent read session after retrying, reducing the chance of stale reads after transient failures.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/efcore#37941](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37941)\\n\\n## Tools warn when used with platform-specific apps\\n\\nThe `dotnet ef` tool now shows a warning when it detects it is being used with a project that targets a platform-specific app model (such as WinForms, WPF, or MAUI). Scaffolding and migration commands run the app in a host process, and platform-specific initialization can interfere. The warning prompts developers to configure a separate design-time factory or use `--no-build`.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/efcore#37868](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37868)\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed a `NullReferenceException` in `SqlServerStringMethodTranslator.TranslateIndexOf` when a parameter is wrapped in a cast expression. ([dotnet/efcore#37956](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37956))\\n- Fixed `ComplexCollection` with `ToJson` generating an incorrect migration default value (`{}` instead of `[]`). ([dotnet/efcore#37965](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37965))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"msbuild.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# MSBuild in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## CLI out-of-proc worker nodes use MSBuild from .NET CLI\\n\\nWhen running `dotnet build` or `dotnet msbuild`, the out-of-process worker nodes now prefer the `MSBuild.dll` distributed with the .NET CLI rather than the one in the global tools path. This ensures all nodes in a multi-process build use the same MSBuild version, reducing version mismatch errors and improving incremental-build correctness.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/msbuild#13452](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13452)\\n\\n## Virtual project references\\n\\nMSBuild now allows targets and tasks to reference virtual projects — in-memory `ProjectInstance` objects that were never written to disk. This enables build tooling and generators to compose and evaluate project graphs without requiring temporary files on the filesystem.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/msbuild#13389](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13389)\\n\\n## Public API for TaskEnvironment construction\\n\\n`TaskEnvironment` — which controls the execution environment for a task — now has a public constructor. Build extensions that host tasks programmatically can now create `TaskEnvironment` instances without reflection.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [dotnet/msbuild#13383](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13383)\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed a `ToolTask` hang when grandchild processes inherit pipe handles from the parent. ([dotnet/msbuild#13351](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13351))\\n- Fixed a race condition in `LoggingService.ProcessLoggingEvent` that could occur after MSBuild shuts down. ([dotnet/msbuild#13450](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13450))\\n- Fixed a race condition in `AssemblyTaskFactory` when registering task types concurrently. ([dotnet/msbuild#13422](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13422))\\n- Fixed macOS symlink handshake mismatch in the .NET task host that caused `MSB4216` errors on case-sensitive volumes. ([dotnet/msbuild#13406](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13406))\\n- Fixed Unix path normalization in MSBuild properties when running in multi-process (`/mt`) mode. ([dotnet/msbuild#13439](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13439))\\n- Fixed `System.IO.File` and `System.IO.Directory` property functions failing with relative paths in `-mt` mode. ([dotnet/msbuild#13239](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13239))\\n- Fixed `%(RecursiveDir)` metadata being lost when tasks run in a task-host process. ([dotnet/msbuild#13318](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13318))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"nuget.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# NuGet in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## File-based app support in the XPlat CLI\\n\\nThe `dotnet nuget` commands now work with file-based apps (single-file C# scripts and `.cs` entry points that use implicit SDK hosting). You can run `dotnet nuget list package`, `dotnet nuget add package`, and other CLI commands against a file-based app without first creating a project file.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [nuget/nuget.client#7169](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7169)\\n\\n## `--allow-untrusted-root` for package signing\\n\\n`dotnet nuget sign` and `nuget sign` gain an `--allow-untrusted-root` flag. When set, signing succeeds even if the certificate chain includes an untrusted root, which is useful in enterprise scenarios with internal certificate authorities that are not in the OS trust store.\\n\\nRelated PRs: [nuget/nuget.client#7201](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7201)\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed `<NuGetAuditSuppress>` with `packages.config` only applying the first suppression entry and ignoring all subsequent ones. ([nuget/nuget.client#7234](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7234))\\n- Fixed `NU1107` error messages not providing correct guidance when Central Package Version Management (CPVM) is used with transitive pinning. ([nuget/nuget.client#7235](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7235))\\n- Fixed path separators being accepted in package alias names, which could cause resolution ambiguity. ([nuget/nuget.client#7244](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7244))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"sdk.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# .NET SDK in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed `NETSDK1005` being incorrectly emitted when a project references another project targeting a different target framework moniker under `dotnet run`. ([dotnet/sdk#53523](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/53523))\\n\\n## Templating\\n\\n- Template engine projects are now NativeAOT-compatible, improving publish times and binary size for tools built on the `Microsoft.TemplateEngine` packages. ([dotnet/templating#10006](https://github.com/dotnet/templating/pull/10006))\\n- Fixed duplicate key handling in template configuration files that could cause template installation to fail silently. ([dotnet/templating#10049](https://github.com/dotnet/templating/pull/10049))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"winforms.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# Windows Forms in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed an `InvalidCastException` in `Control.OnHandleDestroyed` thrown when a control's accessible object is not a `ControlAccessibleObject`. ([dotnet/winforms#14295](https://github.com/dotnet/winforms/pull/14295))\\n- Fixed `ComboBox.ObjectCollection.CopyTo` copying the internal `Entry` wrapper object instead of the actual item value. ([dotnet/winforms#14075](https://github.com/dotnet/winforms/pull/14075))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"wpf.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# Windows Presentation Foundation in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nPreview 3 includes minor infrastructure fixes for WPF. There are no user-facing feature changes in this preview.\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed SDK `.props` file spacing that caused `MSB4281` warnings during WPF project builds. ([dotnet/wpf#11470](https://github.com/dotnet/wpf/pull/11470))\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"csharp.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# C# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nC# 14 compiler work continues in Preview 3. A detailed summary of language changes will be provided in a future preview. See the [Roslyn changelog](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/blob/main/docs/Language%20Feature%20Status.md) for the current status of individual C# 14 features.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"fsharp.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# F# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nF# compiler and tooling improvements continue in Preview 3. A summary of language and library changes will be provided in a future preview as changes stabilize.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"visualbasic.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# Visual Basic in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nThere are no Visual Basic language changes in .NET 11 Preview 3.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"dotnetmaui.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\".NET MAUI release notes are maintained in the [dotnet/maui](https://github.com/dotnet/maui/releases) repository. See the [.NET MAUI Preview 3 release notes](https://github.com/dotnet/maui/releases) for details.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"containers.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\".NET 11 Preview 3 container images are available on [Microsoft Artifact Registry (MCR)](https://mcr.microsoft.com/). See the [dotnet-docker releases](https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet-docker/releases) for details on available image variants.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"11.0.0-preview.3.md\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"# .NET 11 Preview 3 Binaries\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 installers and binaries can be downloaded for the following product versions:\\n\\n- `.NET 11.0.0 Preview 3`\\n- `.NET SDK 11.0.100-preview.3.26170.106`\\n\\nSee [README.md](README.md) for .NET 11 Preview 3 release notes.\\n\\nThe latest .NET releases are always listed at [.NET Releases](../../README.md).\\n\\n## Downloads\\n\\nDownload links will be available when Preview 3 is officially released.\\n\\nYou can check your .NET SDK version by running the following command. The example version shown is for this release.\\n\\n```console\\n$ dotnet --version\\n11.0.100-preview.3.26170.106\\n```\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfiles[\\\"release.json\\\"] = \\\"\\\"\\\"{\\n  \\\"channel-version\\\": \\\"11.0\\\",\\n  \\\"release\\\": {\\n    \\\"release-date\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"release-version\\\": \\\"11.0.0-preview.3\\\",\\n    \\\"security\\\": false,\\n    \\\"cve-list\\\": [],\\n    \\\"release-notes\\\": \\\"https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/11.0.0-preview.3.md\\\",\\n    \\\"runtime\\\": {\\n      \\\"version\\\": \\\"11.0.0-preview.3.26170.106\\\",\\n      \\\"version-display\\\": \\\"11.0.0-preview.3\\\",\\n      \\\"vs-version\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"vs-mac-version\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"sdk\\\": {\\n      \\\"version\\\": \\\"11.0.100-preview.3.26170.106\\\",\\n      \\\"version-display\\\": \\\"11.0.100-preview.3\\\",\\n      \\\"runtime-version\\\": \\\"11.0.0-preview.3.26170.106\\\",\\n      \\\"vs-version\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"vs-mac-version\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfor name, content in files.items():\\n    with open(f\\\"{base}/{name}\\\", \\\"w\\\") as fp:\\n        fp.write(content)\\n\\nprint(\\\"All files written successfully.\\\")\\nfor fn in sorted(os.listdir(base)):\\n    size = os.path.getsize(f\\\"{base}/{fn}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  {fn}: {size} bytes\\\")\\n\"}"
            }
          }
