 are now compiled as runtime-async methods (#126343)\\n- **Unsafe Evolution** — attribute types added for the preview feature (#125721)\\n- **JIT async optimizations** — two continuation-reuse optimizations (#125615, #125869)\\n- **`JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase`** — new System.Text.Json naming policy (#124644)\\n- **Blazor Virtualize variable-height items** — the `Virtualize` component now measures item height dynamically (#64964)\\n- **zstd Content-Encoding** — Zstandard compression in ASP.NET Core (#65479)\\n- **MSBuild CLI worker node fix** — nodes now use MSBuild from .NET CLI (#13452)\\n- **NuGet file-based app CLI support** — `dotnet nuget` commands work with `.cs` file-based apps (#7169)\\n- **EF Core Cosmos session token tracking** — improved failure recovery (#37941)\\n\\n### Open questions / items needing human review\\n\\n1. **C# 14 features** — The Roslyn diff contains ~150 PRs, mostly tooling and test work. Human review needed to identify any user-facing C# 14 language features shipping in Preview 3.\\n2. **F# features** — The F# diff was dominated by agentic workflow infrastructure changes. Human review needed to identify any language/library improvements.\\n3. **Release date** — Preview 3 has not shipped yet (as of this run). The `release.json` has an empty `release-date` field.\\n4. **Binary download links** — `11.0.0-preview.3.md` is a stub pending the official release announcement.\\n5. **Community contributors** — The community contributors section in `runtime.md` is incomplete. PR authors need to be cross-referenced against the GitHub contributor list.\\n6. **NuGet deduplication** — PR nuget/nuget.client#7227 (\\\"Pack is aliased framework aware and supports deduplication\\\") needs clarification on user-facing impact.\\n\\n### Tool setup note\\n\\nThe `release-notes-gen` tool was unavailable this run (no `GITHUB_TOKEN` in environment). The `changes.json` and `features.json` files were not generated via the automated tool; changes were extracted via git log analysis of component repos. A future run with auth available should regenerate these files via `release-notes generate changes`.\\n\"}"
